      "slug": "gram:n3-donna-ni-koto-ka",
      "variants": [],
      "nuance_tags": ["emphasis"],
      "usage_contexts": ["written", "literary", "spoken"],
      "steps_unavailable": "Circumfix around a fixed pre-predicate adverb. The record is explicit (どんなに opens, the predicate goes in plain form, ことか closes: どんなに疲れたことか), but the closed op set has append and no prepend, so an ordered sequence from one base could only emit 疲れたことか and would silently drop the obligatory どんなに slot."
    },
    {
      "slug": "gram:n3-donna-ni-temo",
      "variants": [],
      "nuance_tags": ["concession", "emphasis"],
      "usage_contexts": ["spoken", "written"],
      "steps_unavailable": "Circumfix around a fixed pre-predicate adverb (どんなに + て-form + も; い-adjective くて + も; な-adjective + でも). With no prepend op, any single sequence would emit only the ても half — 書いても, 高くても, 静かでも — which is the separate ても concessive, not this point. Emitting it under this label would teach the wrong pattern."
